\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Held-out test-set point estimates with 95\% cluster-bootstrap confidence intervals (5{,}000 resamples; 30-km $\times $ calendar-day clusters; percentile intervals). Point estimates are computed once on the full test set and are not medians over resamples, so intervals need not be symmetric about them. $\Delta $ rows are differences against the best benchmark in each domain ($T_d = \ensuremath  {0.0\,^{\circ }\mathrm  {C}}$ in CA; $T_d = \ensuremath  {0.5\,^{\circ }\mathrm  {C}}$ in CO). Intervals are conditional on the trained model and realized split.}}{11}{}\protected@file@percent }
